{"game": "mass-effect-andromeda", "language": "english", "appid": 1238000, "month": "2025-11", "window": 2, "start_date": 1762560000, "end_date": 1763251199, "month_true_total": 80, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 22:02:24 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "209327593", "author": {"steamid": "76561197988858484", "personaname": "Roswell Refugee", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Nope90210/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 13, "playtime_forever": 760, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 760, "last_played": 1758487731, "avatar": "5dd7f4939c32c365d92250770502ee8f1989a6ee"}, "language": "english", "review": "Major con - EA launcher. If I buy it through Steam, it should launch through Steam.\nBut it's not like EA has a track record of listening to their customers.\n\nIf you enjoyed M.E. 1-3 then you'll likely find this to be \"meh\"\nThe puzzles are incredibly annoying. It's kinda like sudoku, but different in a stupid way.\n\nLooks decent, has tons of bugs. Enough bugs to make me stop playing after about 10 hours.\nMaybe I'll get bored and pick it back up eventually, but probably not.\n\nTo sum it up, it's FAR from being worth the $40 I see it's going for at the time of writing this review. I think I got it on sale like a year ago for really cheap, so I'm not super upset.\nNeed to remind myself that EA games even at a steep discount, are still not worth it.", "timestamp_created": 1763242816, "timestamp_updated": 1763242816, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 20, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.58236539363861084", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "209317370", "author": {"steamid": "76561198130562122", "personaname": "Shockwave", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://